-- Lexical mistakes. The lexer reports these against the range of source the mistake covers, so
-- they carry a location just like the parser's own diagnostics do.

-- A string literal that is not terminated before the end of the line.
fn unterminated() = "abc

-- A string gap that is not closed by a second '\'.
fn unclosedGap() = "abc\ def"

-- Characters that are not tokens in the language. Each byte is reported on its own, so a
-- copy-pasted quote or dash produces one diagnostic per byte of its encoding.
fn smartQuote() = “abc”

-- The declaration after the above still parses.
fn after(a: Int) = a

-- A nested block comment that is never terminated. This one has to come last: it runs to the end
-- of the file, so anything after it is part of the comment.
{- outer {- inner -}
fn insideComment() = 0
